// @name: BP — Graphics
// @tagline: six notes, legato and staccato
// @description: A short Bol Processor grammar (2020) from Bernard Bel's corpus stacking legato and staccato articulations across three simultaneous voices (six notes total). Derived by BPx and played through Kanopi's WebAudio transport. Ctrl+Enter to derive, Ctrl+. to hush.
// @language: bp3
// @outputs: audio
// @level: didactic
// @tags: articulation
//
// Bol Processor BP3 compatible with version BP2.9.8
// Grammar file saved as "-gr.tryGraphics". Date: 2020-10-17 02:51:08
-se.tryGraphics

gram#1[1] S --> {_legato(20) C4 D4 E4, _staccato(10) F#5 G3, - G4}

// Legato will not be applied to E4 because it is the last note in the sequence.
// Try this grammar with settings piano roll and not piano roll…
